WEBVTT

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:05.760
Ow...

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.000
You okay?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.020
Fine.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.610
Hard head.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.650
Okay.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.610
Drinks after work?

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.550
I don't drink.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.120
Aren't you an adult?

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.370
Don't get drunk, so don't like it.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.000
All about mindset. Enjoy it.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.520
Wouldn't mind food.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.510
Deal.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.630
A car.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.890
Hey, new guy. Check it out.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.130
R-Right.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.090
It's made out of spare parts.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.390
A suicide bomber?

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.590
Shall we fire?

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.760
Nah, let's wait and see.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.720
We'll deem it a threat if 
it accelerates toward us.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.390
Roger.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.140
Overthinking it, huh?

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.810
Oh? Different convoy approaching.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.010
Check it out.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:07.120
Danger!

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.350
Return fire!

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.270
Bond! What are you doing?!

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.910
Bond, if it's too hard...

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.490
No, I'll do it.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:49.620
<i>On that day,</i>

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.840
<i>I killed someone for the first time.</i>

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.660
Hurry up!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.640
Episode 17
"Earth-Saving Hunter"

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.940
<i>I was an awkward kid...</i>

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:38.100
<i>One who never really fit in.</i>

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.910
<i>And years passed without anything changing.</i>

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.530
And that was friggin' hilarious, man!

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.040
What?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:54.920
Nothing.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.180
<i>I'd clearly failed to become a 
functional member of society.</i>

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.720
<i>I felt suffocated.</i>

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.940
<i>During those years,</i>

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.240
<i>I basically flailed my way through 
each day like a fish out of water.</i>

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.900
<i>Life seemed like torture.</i>

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:24.520
While we know our environment 
is being damaged,

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.380
we can't even figure out the exact cause.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.470
The environment is far too complex a system.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:35.130
For example, a massive outbreak of insects...

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.350
<i>Martel Group Japan,</i>

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.780
<i>a scientific organization that focused 
on environmental protection.</i>

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.080
<i>As members, my parents participated 
in its activities with zeal,</i>

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.680
<i>and they even brought me along.</i>

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:55.910
Kotarou-kun.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:57.580
Iko-san?

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.760
<i>Fuku Iko-san, caretaker at an 
orphanage called House of Ties.</i>

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.700
<i>She'd asked me to help 
with something simple.</i>

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.760
Late?

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:06.690
Yeah.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.720
These kids kept dawdling.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:09.910
Sorry.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.880
I'm the only one around today.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.020
So, what do you want me to do?

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.080
Watch over her.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.170
Pa.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.860
I have to take these two to day care.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.510
Take care of the rest.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.120
Uh, what's your name?

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.280
Pa.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.640
Not that.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.460
Pa?

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.130
I'm not your pa.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.930
I'm Tennouji Kotarou.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.440
Pa.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:42.880
Well, crap...

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.690
I'm back!

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.020
Oh, are you two friends now?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.820
We can't even hold a conversation.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.520
Normally she's almost too energetic,

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.500
but I see she's well-behaved today.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.580
Is it because you're sitting with Kotarou?

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.690
She calls me Pa.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.790
That's the only word she knows.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:07.810
If you don't mind, could you let her 
sit with you during the seminar, too?

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.320
I guess.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.090
Thanks.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.470
Got a name?

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:12.850
I'm Iko-chan!

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.060
Not you.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:15.850
Her.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.340
Oh.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.350
Her name

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.170
is Senri Akane-chan.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.860
How about the environmental 
aftereffects of the H-bombs?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.610
As of today, the islands' ecosystem 
has almost completely recovered.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:36.770
It's said that it takes centuries for the 
radioactive effects of H-bombs to die down.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.770
You'll fall off.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:41.500
We will now take questions from the audience.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:43.930
Ask them something, Kotarou.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.600
Not today.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.700
I told you to prepare!

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.260
Come on, raise your hand.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.260
I said not today.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.610
As part of our family, you 
have to follow our rules!

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.760
Stop it!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.370
What's your question, young man?

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:05.900
Basically, humanity is the biggest obstacle 
to protecting the environment, right?

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.810
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:15.520
Huh?

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.070
Your cheek...

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.550
Did they get mad at you?

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.940
My parents did, yeah.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.830
And they hit me.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.050
Thanks for today.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:28.670
Whatever.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.660
What you said earlier wasn't off the mark.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:37.310
Humanity is of pretty much no 
benefit to the environment.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.480
We've strayed too far from 
Mother Nature's embrace.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:46.370
Some say we eventually won't be 
able to live on Earth anymore.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:49.090
Say, Kotarou-kun.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.200
Has anything painful happened to you?

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.040
Sure.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.700
Countless things.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.100
If humanity gets culled in the future 
and all the painful things go away,

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.460
wouldn't you feel a lot better?

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.840
Of course, life will continue to exist.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.960
Though it might not include humanity.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.400
You're not getting away.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.050
In here, huh?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.380
A bloodsucking worm, huh?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.680
A dangerous creature like you 
can't be allowed to roam free.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.590
Earth is in grave danger,

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:55.760
and it needs the help of 
the Earth-Saving Hunter.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.220
That said,

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.770
this thing is just small fry.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.950
I'll give you what you want.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.280
Take my blood.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.270
It's like a tsuchinoko from the legends.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.470
Is it good?

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.540
But that's it for you.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.660
I can freely control my blood.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:19.860
There.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.380
You just swallowed a thousand needles!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.330
Tonight's Earth Saving is complete.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.460
<i>What were those monsters?</i>

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.240
<i>Why do I have these powers?</i>

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.500
<i>None of that mattered to me.</i>

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.770
<i>I just take out UMAs as 
the Earth-Saving Hunter.</i>

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.260
<i>I'd gotten addicted to that thrill.</i>

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.620
<i>I figured out that most of 
the UMAs were in the forest.</i>

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:56.600
<i>And the Earth-Saving Hunter moved 
his base of operations there.</i>

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.830
Tonight's Earth Saving is complete.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:12.110
<i>I need more power.</i>

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.590
<i>I guess I'll go with that.</i>

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.590
<i>Give me strength befitting 
the Earth-Saving Hunter.</i>

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.400
<i>For some reason, ever since I was a kid,</i>

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:43.090
<i>I had the power to do anything I wished.</i>

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:03.910
What the...

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:09.560
It's pretty.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.000
Meanwhile, I'm...

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:22.300
I wish everything would just melt away.

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.450
Environmental activism, my ass!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:30.330
Nobody cares!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.720
They're not ostriches.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.220
Dinosaurs?

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.010
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.100
<i>Am I gonna die here?</i>

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.360
<i>Whatever.</i>

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:04.720
<i>That's fine by me.</i>

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.990
<i>I'm not scared of dying.</i>

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.270
Is he a civilian?

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:26.030
Seems to be just a kid.

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:28.560
What do we do now?

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.800
Our team specializes in hunting.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.640
We don't walk around with first aid kits.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.270
Wait. There's something off about him.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.980
The bleeding's stopped.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:46.740
Sleep, boy.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:56.120
This your wallet?

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.760
Thank you! Let me offer 
you something in return.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.760
Don't bother. Just get going.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.340
Uh, how did you get so strong?

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.040
Do you practice martial arts?

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.870
What kind of rock do you listen to?

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.020
Sorry to summon you here.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.250
It's okay.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.200
That aside—

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.000
Oh, right.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.660
Here's your phone we picked up in the forest.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.360
Thank you.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:36.010
Uh, who are you people, Esaka-san?

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:41.010
We're investigating UMAs 
at the university's request.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.500
Like those dinosaurs?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:46.740
No, those were just large birds.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:50.140
You were fighting with swords 
and axes, weren't you?

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:51.930
Of course not.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.860
The others were staff members 
and vets from the zoo.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.440
And I'm a bird watcher myself.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.940
I'm helping them because 
I know a lot about birds.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.540
By the way...

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:06.070
What were you doing in 
the forest, Tennouji-kun?

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:07.840
I was out for a walk.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.260
So late at night?

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:10.430
That's not safe.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.700
I'm used to it.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.910
But you should stop doing
that from now on.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.020
I will.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:16.820
Good.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.840
One more thing.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.320
That forest is home to several new species.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.970
I want you to keep that a secret 
until we finish investigating.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:26.750
Sure.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.400
I won't tell anyone.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.090
I don't have any friends to tell, anyway.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:35.350
There are no contacts on this phone, either.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.030
I see.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:39.850
In that case, add me.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:44.440
Why don't you become email pals with me?

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.570
<b>Esaka-san</b>

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:57.410
Hello.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.740
Thanks for having us.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.430
They're our neighbors, the Kanbes.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:01.580
Say hello.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:02.980
Hey.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:05.090
Sorry our son is so unsociable.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:07.420
That's just how boys are.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.100
Go on, Kotori.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.420
Say hi.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.530
I'm Kanbe Kotori.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.720
Nice to meet you.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.220
Yeah.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.600
<i>We've met in passing several times, though.</i>

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.250
We're going out with them for a bit.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:22.840
Take care of Kotori-chan.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:32.700
Thanks for having me, Kotarou-kun.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:37.830
Want something to drink?

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.330
Don't mind me.

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.070
Feel free to take whatever you want.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.840
Thanks.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:48.520
You're in grade school, right?

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.090
Yeah.

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:53.270
Oh.

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:55.220
Anyway, I'll be in my room.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:56.720
Irresponsible brat.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.910
I see you have sharp ears.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.880
Since you're so proficient at violence,

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:04.210
I suppose your senses are sharp, as well.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.690
You saw me?

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:06.770
Yes.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.940
I hate violence, so I found you to be scum.

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:12.160
They picked a fight with me.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.310
That's not right.

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:15.700
They were picking on another kid.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.580
You stuck your nose in it yourself.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.440
You...

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:21.620
What is it?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.340
Is this what you're really like?

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:24.450
What of it?

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:25.390
Nothing.

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:28.260
You just seem to really 
be looking down on me.

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:29.600
I don't seem like it.

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:31.090
I am looking down on you.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.480
That so?

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:36.380
Well, have fun up on your little high horse.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:37.900
I'll be in my room.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.800
Don't call me unless you need something.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:41.760
I won't.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:45.730
Thank you for your time.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:48.730
Next up...

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.570
Hey there, baby wonder.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.740
Stop calling me that.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.940
Which part? Baby or wonder?

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:00.220
Both.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:01.490
Well, aren't you demanding?

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:05.060
So, how about Martel, huh?

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:05.970
What about it?

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:07.500
What are your thoughts?

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.480
That seminar wasn't at all scientific.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:13.540
They're basically saying we 
should accept natural disaster

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:15.510
wiping out civilization.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.700
Calling it natural selection...

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:23.270
It feels like they're playing on anxiety 
and questioning people's right to live.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.960
This place is messed up.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.520
Never thought we'd agree on something.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.240
You should head back.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.400
This is my exclusive box seat.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:35.450
Why don't you take part?

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.910
Because it's a pain.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:38.270
Lies.

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:39.550
You're running away, aren't you?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.530
If you don't like it, then just quit.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.900
There's more to it, like my 
relationship with my parents.

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:45.460
That's what you call runnin—

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.390
Yeah, yeah, keep talking.

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:49.670
You're wasting time running 
away from making a decision.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.260
I won't run away like you.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.330
<i>From that day on,</i>

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:57.760
<i>the Kanbes stopped taking 
part in Martel activities.</i>

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.130
<i>She kept her word and did 
what she said she'd do.</i>

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:04.060
What's that filthy dog?

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:05.430
Pero.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:06.420
Make him move.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:07.630
I can't go in.

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:08.910
I'm sorry.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:10.000
He just won't move.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.940
Fine. I'll make him.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.280
Outta the way...

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.640
Ow!

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.460
Screw you!

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.200
Don't be rough with him!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.320
Stop the dog, not me!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.330
Please, Pero! Let him go!

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.190
I hope you've vaccinated him for rabies.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.130
I have.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.780
I'll pay for your treatment, too.

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:30.970
No need.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:31.780
Let me!

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.090
Just, please don't call the pound.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:38.970
Do you love that filthy, violent dog so much?

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.970
He's been through some horrible things...

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.010
Oh?

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:46.980
So even Miss Baby Wonder 
can sympathize with dogs.

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:51.760
Well, I didn't get hurt 
too badly, so it's fine.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:54.630
Just keep him away from my front door.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:55.480
He's an eyesore.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.270
Okay...

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:04.870
<i>Apparently, that dog had been 
abused by his previous owner.</i>

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.980
<i>And the Kanbes took him in.</i>

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:11.360
<i>He contracted food poisoning when 
they gave him something with onions,</i>

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.790
<i>and now he was too wary to even eat.</i>

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.130
<i>But Kotori was doing her 
best to take care of him.</i>

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:22.640
<b>Missing Dog</b>

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.580
That dog went missing, huh?

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:26.920
When?

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:28.050
Last night.

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.700
Looks like he ripped off his collar.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.470
It had his fur and blood on it.

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:34.520
Talk about a great escape.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.650
Please let us know if you see him.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.290
He'll probably go back to the wild.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.780
The forest's right there, after all.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.630
Pero's been a pet all his life.

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:45.990
He can't find his own food.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:48.120
His legs aren't in perfect condition, either.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:52.750
When I told my parents to quit 
Martel, they made me promise

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.380
to take care of Pero.

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:08.510
What do you want?

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:09.510
Hey.

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:10.870
I brought you something.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:15.150
What is it?

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.800
What do you mean?

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.400
Seriously, what?

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.160
Horned beetle larvae?!

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:23.660
Are you going to say they look like chili 
shrimp and make me unable to eat it?!

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:24.880
Stop it.

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:26.780
<i>I</i> won't be able to eat chili shrimp anymore.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.980
It's what you're looking for.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:34.430
Whoa, there.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.790
Hurry up and bring his collar.

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:38.420
Where did you find him?

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:40.780
I went on a stroll through the forest

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.860
and happened to find him 
occupying my box seat.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.710
So I decided to complain to the owner—

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.660
Thank goodness.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:03.150
He ate it.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:06.060
Maybe he likes his food a little wet.

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.400
I never tried that.

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:09.360
Later.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.200
My job here is done.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:12.970
Wait.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:15.930
Are you gonna give me a wad of cash?

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.050
I'm kidding.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.270
I don't want any.

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:21.210
Thanks.

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:24.310
I said thanks.

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:25.200
Oh...

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:26.580
Well...

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:28.340
Shouldn't you look at me when you say that?

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:31.540
Not that I care.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.540
When it comes to idly staying in one place,

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.010
I guess I'm the same as him.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:48.180
<i>Pero didn't live long after that.</i>

00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:51.140
<i>And, until the end, he never took to anyone.</i>

00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:03.680
<i>Even after what happened,</i>

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:06.850
<i>my relationship with Kotori 
didn't change much.</i>

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:10.560
<i>But it did affect me in a way.</i>

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:15.800
<i>Looking at her love a dog 
that was just a duty to her</i>

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:17.560
<i>suddenly made me anxious.</i>

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:21.950
I'll quit Martel.

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:28.050
<i>My instincts were screaming 
at me to move forward.</i>
